"""The tables in the code region ($0-$1C601): every place the disassembler's code/data map
(tools/fixpoint.sh) has data, jump tables included (the C reads their offsets as data), split at
each address an instruction points at, less what other files already hold (the palettes); and
two exceptions, named so (docs/EXTRACT.md, "The tables in the code region"). All of them, not
only those the runs were seen to read (--rom-reads), so a path no run reached finds its table.

Only the addresses, sizes and names are here: the bytes are the ROM's, written out by
tools/extract.py into assets/tables/code_tables.json and built back by tools/rebuild.py.

(address, length, element: 'b' bytes, 'w' words, 'l' longs, name, routines that point at it, note)
"""

